# LF everywhere, in the repo AND in every checkout, whatever core.autocrlf says (owner,
# 2026-10-01: "use LF standardly throughout"; "CRLF is a continual issue"). Git for Windows'
# default core.autocrlf=true would otherwise check text out as CRLF: `sh` then fails on the
# trailing \r (cmem/known-issues.md KI-1), and exact-text matching (tools/filc/patch-pass.ts,
# src/stdpatch.zig) breaks.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files: never converted.
*.o binary
*.a binary
*.so binary
*.xz binary
*.zip binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.wasm binary
